WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:06.000
♪♪

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.200
-Wow! Nothing like first snow of the winter.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.734
-Wow, man. The tree looks great, doesn't it?

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.000
-It's beautiful.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.901
♪♪

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:25.801
♪♪

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.100
-Well, want to help me carry it to the curb?

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.701
-Sure, man.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.734
[ Chain saw buzzing ]

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.167
-From Studio 6B in Rockefeller Center

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.801
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.801
it's "The Tonight Show starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.567
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.234
-Tonight, join Jimmy and his guests --

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.200
the co-hosts of "Queer Eye"...

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.000
JB Smoove...

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.934
comedian Matthew Broussard...

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:57.901
and featuring the legendary Roots crew.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:00.501
-1579!

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.767
-And now, here he is!

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:07.467
Jimmy Fallon!

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.234
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪ -♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.033
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪ -♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:18.367
-I love you. Thank you. Awesome!

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:22.267
Thank you very much. Hi. I see you. Thank you.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.534
Yes. I love you! I see you. Thank you very much.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.934
♪♪

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:32.267
Oh! Wow! That's the energy right there.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.834
Welcome, everybody.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.734
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.934
Thank you for being here. Thank you for watching.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.567
Well guys, today New York City got hit

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.133
with the first big snowstorm of the year.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.834
It's always so beautiful in the morning.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:50.267
Then by noon it's like walking through a frappuccino.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.834
Thankfully, I got to the office without a problem.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.767
Outside I saw a guy shoveling Sixth Avenue,

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:56.934
and I said, "Thank you.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.467
Thank you so much, Mr. de Blasio."

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.901
And this was strange.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.767
On the way in, I passed by a bunch of snowmen

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.901
on the sidewalk, and then I realized they were just people

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.100
who had been standing in line for rapid tests.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.133
It's not just New York, though.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.133
A massive snowstorm also hit Kentucky,

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.467
and a bunch of cars got stuck on the highway.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.400
Luckily, one guy seemed to be in pretty good spirits.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.000
Watch this.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.334
-Hey, it's Father Jim reporting live on Interstate 75.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.968
It's pretty bad, and so we've been here now

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.367
about two and a half hours.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:34.100
And thank God the bourbon fairy came by.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.100
-Thank God. The bourbon fairy. -The bourbon fairy.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.234
-Yeah, right after that, he got a visit from the D.U.I. fairy.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.734
Yup, that's Father Jim from the Church of the Heavenly Buzz.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:52.200
Meanwhile, I heard about a man in Texas

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.234
who was arrested after allegedly driving drunk

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:58.133
with a lit barbecue pit in the back of his truck.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.868
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:03.200
Now, in Texas, a man drunk, driving a lit barbecue,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.901
is actually the state bird.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.267
Yeah. That's correct.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:11.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.501
[ Laughs ] It's the state bird.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.133
Let's get to some news.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.534
The White House is finalizing plans for the Postal Service

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:19.901
to deliver 500 million rapid tests

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.901
straight to people's homes. Yup.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.100
It is the first time anyone said the words "Postal Service"

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.834
and "rapid" in the same sentence.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.067
Asked why he chose the Postal Service,

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:31.901
Biden said, "I want everyone to have them before Christmas."

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.100
Mr. President, here is my advice.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.701
You want to get 500 million tests out

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:39.434
right away? Forget the post office.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:40.834
Domino's.

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.334
That pizza tracker is accurate!

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.701
[ Applause ]

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.501
That's right. The White House plans to send

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:51.501
at-home COVID tests to Americans as soon as next week,

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.334
but not everyone knows how they work.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.801
I've had to test a lot recently,

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.434
and so let me just break down how to interpret the results.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:04:00.834
For example, one line means you tested negative.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:04.200
However, two lines mean you tested positive.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.501
Up next, if you get three lines, you have a new variant

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.200
and they'll probably name it after you.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.467
Meanwhile, four lines mean

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.167
you've been to Florida in the past two weeks.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:17.100
And finally, if you get an X, it means

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.000
you stuck the nasal swab in the wrong hole.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.667
I hope that helps. I --

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.033
-The wrong hole.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.667
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.701
-Hey, I read that Twitter is testing a new feature

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:32.067
that lets you react to other people's tweets

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:33.968
with a short video.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.534
Yeah. I fell like we're a day away

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:38.234
from Twitter just renaming itself TwitTwok.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.567
But the videos are easy to post.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.434
You just open the app, tap on the camera,

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.300
and then verify that you're not Donald Trump

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.501
or Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.000
That's all. Very easy.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:54.634
Very easy to do. Anyone can do it.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.834
Speaking of Trump, I saw that he plans to launch

00:04:56.834 --> 00:05:01.434
his own social-media app in February on Presidents' Day.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.968
This is real. The app is called Truth Social.

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:08.133
And he said it's different than other social-media platforms.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.067
For example, you can't send a tweet.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.400
but you can send a...

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.834
-Bing, bing, bong, bong, bing, bing, bing.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.901
-And when you get a notification, it sounds like...

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.968
[ Horn honking ]

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.801
When asked what else is different about his app,

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.267
Trump said...

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:27.634
-It's tremendously big and tremendously wet.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:31.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:34.968
-When asked who can use the app he said everyone, including...

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:40.934
-Person, woman, man, camera, TV.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:44.734
-But you can only use the app if you agree to show...

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:47.868
-Total respect for Donald Trump

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:52.534
and for Donald Trump's very, very large a-brain.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:56.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.834
-Trump actually has an account already.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.934
Of course, the first person he followed was...

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.367
-Russia, Russia, Russia, Russia!

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:07.234
-He also posted his very first message. It said...

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:09.767
-God bless the United Shtatesh.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.868
-There you go. Well, that's --

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:14.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.901
Should be a fun time.

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.300
Hey, listen to this.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.467
In South Korea's presidential election,

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:22.801
one candidate pushed for government-funded

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:24.267
hair-loss treatments

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:27.634
and has gained the support of a lot of bald voters.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.567
Yeah, it's the first time a politician's been praised

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:31.367
for staging a massive cover-up.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.033
Hey, according to a new survey,

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:38.534
on average, men rate themselves a 5.9 out of 10

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:41.234
on the attractiveness scale.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:44.133
Women heard and were like, "Ugh. Inflation strikes again."

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:45.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:47.934
"Good for you."

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.701
[ Applause ]

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:52.501
Well, get this. A group of Canadian influencers

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:55.334
filmed themselves partying maskless on a flight,

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:56.868
sparked a huge public outrage,

00:06:56.868 --> 00:06:58.701
and now they're all stuck in Mexico

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:02.067
because airlines are refusing to fly them home.

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:04.467
Yeah. What better way to teach someone a lesson

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:07.167
than forcing them to spend more time in Cancun?

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:12.701
"These frozen drinks are for you guys, too, you knuckleheads!

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:16.100
Learn your lesson. Never do that again.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:20.033
Bottomless margis."

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:23.534
Finally, a man in Nebraska took an at-home DNA test

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:27.467
and was surprised to find out he has 18 half-siblings.

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:29.467
-[ Audience oohs ] -He was shocked.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:33.067
Mostly because he thought he was taking a COVID test.

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.834
Yeah, it was an at-home DNA test,

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:37.667
so he can't be sure they're his siblings

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:40.634
until the PCR results come back. We have a great show.

